  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Lit Signal Box",
    "overview": "The console is a railway signal box that runs a local proxy. The request route is drawn as a lit track diagram across the top bar: client, then proxy, then each gateway in precedence order, with account lamps on each gateway. Views are numbered levers in a frame on the left. Labels are engraved traffolyte plates. The metaphor does work: an exhausted quota is a track occupied in red, a blocked gateway is a danger lamp, and a healthy console reads as unlit enamel with a few clear lamps.\n\nThe surfaces are enamel. Day is a pale grey-green box; night is a near-black box. Nothing floats, nothing glows, nothing is glass. Depth comes from 1px hairlines, 1.5px ink borders and tonal steps between ground, panel and sunk enamel, not from shadow. Density is operator-grade: each view has one deciding figure at poster size (44px), everything else sits at reading size, and tables use tabular figures so columns of quota can be compared at a glance.\n\nConfirmed rejections: the dark sidebar with stat cards, provider hues (purple Claude, blue Google, cyan Kimi), gradients, glow or blur on surfaces, and rounded-lg/xl/full corners. Motion is short and rare: lamps and track fills change in 160 to 400 ms, and nothing loops except loading indicators.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat enamel surfaces with a 2px radius; no shadow at rest.",
      "Colour is a lamp: clear, caution, danger, off. Green only marks a completed action.",
      "Traffolyte plates (Barlow Semi Condensed, capitals) name providers, sources and view levers.",
      "Track circuits show quota on one fixed 0 to 100% scale; an exhausted pool fills its whole circuit red.",
      "A route mimic in the top bar shows the request path and the reason each signal shows its aspect.",
      "Two boxes, one token set: day and night resolve from `data-sb-theme` on `<html>`."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Settle Rule",
        "body": "Lamps and track fills change in 160 to 400 ms with the shared ease curve. Nothing loops except an in-flight spinner and the first-load skeleton.",
        "section": "overview"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lamp-Only Colour Rule",
        "body": "Hue appears only as a lamp or a state wash that names a real state. Everything else is ink on enamel. Providers, families and brands are told apart by plates and text, never by colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Green-Means-Done Rule",
        "body": "Green (`lamp-ok`, `ok`, `ok-wash`) marks a completed action such as a saved setting or a passed test. Healthy is clear white, not green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Deciding Figure Rule",
        "body": "Each view has exactly one `.figure`. Everything else is reading size.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Plate Is For Names Rule",
        "body": "Plate capitals name a provider, a source, a stable short code, a lever, or a state word in a tag. Plates are not for sentences and are not for every label.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is Data Rule",
        "body": "IBM Plex Mono is for values the operator copies or compares. It is never used for prose or for field labels, except code-like names such as environment variables.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Frozen Utility Rule",
        "body": "`css/style.css` is a frozen Tailwind/DaisyUI build with no config. Markup may use only its layout utilities (display, flex, grid, gap, padding, margin, width, height, overflow, hidden, and the responsive variants that exist in that file). Every colour, type and component rule is hand-written in `css/signalbox.css` against `var(--sb-*)`. A class missing from `style.css` does nothing, so check it exists before using it. The legacy colour and component rules in `style.css` (`btn-action-*`, `standard-table`, `status-pill-*`, `bg-space-*`, `text-neon-*`) are not to be used in markup.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-At-Rest Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces carry no shadow at rest. Lift is a hairline or an ink border. A shadow appears only on a layer above the page.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Device Gradient Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces, buttons and text never use gradients. Gradients are allowed only to draw a device: a lamp's lit lens (radial), the 5% graduation marks on a track (repeating linear), the dotted off-segment in the route, and the two chevrons of a select.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Calm-At-Rest Rule",
        "body": "A healthy row is plain ink. Trouble gets a lamp, a tag and a wash, and where the view supports sorting it sorts first.",
        "section": "components"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lamp Beside Words Rule",
        "body": "A lamp always sits next to text that names the state. Colour is never the only carrier of meaning.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do route every colour through a token: `var(--sb-*)`. Known literals that remain: `#fff` on Danger Fill (buttons and `plate-danger`), `#b22d18` for the night danger-button hover, and `#1b1c19` on the caution plate.",
      "Do pair each lamp or tag with the word that names its state.",
      "Do give each view one `.figure` at 44px and keep everything else at reading size.",
      "Do keep healthy rows plain ink; reserve `tr.is-blocked`, danger tags and danger lamps for trouble.",
      "Do express every quota as a `.track` on the fixed 0 to 100% scale, with its percentage and reset time as text.",
      "Do use a 2px radius, 1px hairlines for dividers, 1.5px ink borders for controls, and dashed borders for disabled.",
      "Do keep motion between 160ms and 400ms, and respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (already global).",
      "Do wrap any table that can overflow in `.table-wrap`.",
      "Do draw icons from the outline SVG set: 24px viewBox, 2px stroke, `currentColor`.",
      "Do check that a layout class exists in `style.css` before using it; put all other styling in `signalbox.css`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a gradient, glow, blur or decorative shadow to a surface. Gradients are for lamp lenses, track graduations, the route's off-segment and the select chevrons only.",
      "Don't colour a family, provider or brand. Use a plate and text.",
      "Don't use green for a healthy state. Green marks a completed action only.",
      "Don't nest a `.panel` inside a `.panel`.",
      "Don't set prose or field labels in mono. Mono is for IDs, emails, URLs, keys, log lines and JSON.",
      "Don't use Tailwind colour classes, DaisyUI colour modifiers, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-xl`, `rounded-full`, `shadow-*`, `backdrop-blur`, or any `bg-space-*`, `text-neon-*`, `text-gray-*` or `text-white` class in markup or in JS strings that build classes.",
      "Don't add a hue to tell chart series apart. Use the ink ramp and dash patterns.",
      "Don't put Label Ink text on Pressed Enamel in the day box (4.2:1).",
      "Don't hand-write a colour or type value in a view. If a value is missing, add a token to `css/signalbox.css` in both boxes."
    ]
  }
}
